; companion to capture-avoidance-blocks-unsound-instantiation.kurt: the *same* premise
; must still let a genuinely safe instantiation through -- substituting the outer `x`
; with a fresh, unrelated constant `c` involves no capture at all, and should succeed
; exactly like it would on paper. This confirms the previous file's rejection is really
; about capture-avoidance, not some unrelated limitation silently blocking this whole
; shape of derivation.
load logic
load equality
const c
use forall x (exists y (not (x = y)))
exists y (not (c = y))
